[h1]Recurring Diplomacy — Changelog[/h1]

One bullet per change. Newest first.

Keep every entry short and non-technical: what actually changes for the player in the game.
No file, class or engine names, no engine reasoning - that belongs in a code comment.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]1.1[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]New: start an action as soon as you can afford it.[/b] When you are short of Influence, an hourglass appears beside the price. Click it and the action starts at the beginning of the first turn you can pay for it - once. To keep it running after that, use the sync button as before.
[*][b]Works on independent powers too[/b], so you can queue befriending an independent power the moment you have the Influence for it.
[*][b]The hourglass only shows where it makes sense:[/b] not on an action you already have running, not on actions where you still have to pick a target, and never on sanctions or war.
[*][b]Influence prices are now chips[/b], in the same style as Better City UI: gold when you can start the action, greyed when you cannot. Clicking a gold price starts the action, like clicking its row.
[*][b]The turn summary also lists independent powers[/b], by name and with the action's icon. What you started there is shown in blue, like espionage, since nobody has to agree to it.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]1.0[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]First release.[/b]
[*][b]A sync button beside every treaty, endeavour and espionage action[/b] on a leader's Diplomacy screen. Gold and glowing = kept running with this leader, grey = not.
[*][b]Switching it on starts the action at once[/b] if the game allows it now; afterwards it is proposed again at the start of your turn whenever it has run out.
[*][b]Respects the game's limits.[/b] Treaties can be kept running with every leader; endeavours and espionage only with as many leaders at once as the game allows (Benjamin Franklin gets an extra endeavour). When the limit is full the button is locked and its tooltip names the leader it runs with - [b]Shift+click[/b] moves it to the leader you are talking to.
[*][b]A short summary at the start of your turn[/b] lists what was renewed, grouped by leader with their portrait: green - agreed, red - refused, grey - no answer yet, blue - espionage. It stays on screen while the cursor is over it.
[*][b]Saved with your game[/b] - loading an older save brings back exactly the choices it had.
[*][b]In 12 languages[/b]: English, German, Spanish, French, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, Ukrainian (shown when the game is set to Russian), Simplified and Traditional Chinese.
[/list]
